 "response": "Tepi's budget is **$2022K**.\n\n**Approach**\n- Only Finance Office records count. Messages from Sales, Legal, Operations, the PMO and the others do not change the budget.\n- I followed each chain of withdrawals to its last link. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so the update it targeted still applies. For example, the chain #1545 \u2192 #0504 \u2192 #0031 \u2192 #0018 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0002 ends with #0002 withdrawn. The chain #0920 \u2192 #0331 \u2192 #0176 \u2192 #0119 \u2192 #0110 \u2192 #0084 \u2192 #0078 \u2192 #0069 \u2192 #0035 ends with #0035 still applying.\n- About 115 Finance Office budget updates end up withdrawn and count as never having happened. Two of these, #0261 (withdrawn by #0978) and #0435 (withdrawn by #1225), I initially missed and then corrected.\n- Starting from the $1810K set in #0001, I applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in order.\n\n**Running total at a few points**\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0100 | $3146K |\n| #0509 | $825K |\n| #0711 | $1760K |\n| #1250 | $2592K |\n| #1596 | $2022K |\n\nThis was a long running sum done by hand in one pass, and I did not run a second independent check.\n\nANSWER: $2022K",
